T*
(ACME PETROCHEMICAL DEMO COMPLEX - CORPORATE PROCESS SAFETY STANDARD) Tj
T*
(DOCUMENT CODE: STD-PHA-001 | REVISION: R1 | MANDATORY GOVERNANCE PROCEDURE) Tj
T*
(TITLE: PROCESS HAZARD ANALYSIS \(PHA\), 5x5 RISK RANKING MATRIX & HAZOP STUDY PROCEDURE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. PURPOSE & SCOPE) Tj
T*
(This standard defines the mandatory corporate methodology for conducting Hazard and Operability \(HAZOP\) studies, Layer of Protection Analysis \(LOPA\), and 5x5 Risk Matrix severity/likelihood evaluations across all exothermic chemical units \(including Unit 2300 CHP Concentration and Cleavage\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. CORPORATE 5x5 RISK RANKING MATRIX) Tj
T*
(Severity Categories \(Consequence to Personnel, Environment, and Plant Assets\):) Tj
T*
(- Severity 5 \(Catastrophic\): Uncontained runaway reaction, vessel rupture, or toxic/flammable release with potential fatalities or > $50M asset loss.) Tj
T*
(- Severity 4 \(Major\): Major loss of primary containment \(LOPC\), permanent disability, or $5M - $50M plant damage.) Tj
T*
(- Severity 3 \(Serious\): Lost-time injury, localized fire/spill, or PSV lift to closed relief system \($500k - $5M\).) Tj
T*
(- Severity 2 \(Minor\): Recordable first-aid event or minor equipment outage \($50k - $500k\).) Tj
T*
(- Severity 1 \(Negligible\): Process upset within design envelope \(< $50k\).) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
