T*
(STD-PHA-001 PAGE 2 OF 5 - LIKELIHOOD LEVELS & RISK TIER CLASSIFICATION) Tj
T*
(Likelihood Categories \(Initiating Event Frequency\):) Tj
T*
(- Likelihood E \(Frequent\): > 1 event per year \(> 10^-1 /yr\)) Tj
T*
(- Likelihood D \(Probable\): 10^-2 to 10^-1 events/yr) Tj
T*
(- Likelihood C \(Occasional\): 10^-3 to 10^-2 events/yr) Tj
T*
(- Likelihood B \(Remote\): 10^-4 to 10^-3 events/yr) Tj
T*
(- Likelihood A \(Improbable\): < 10^-4 events/yr) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Risk Tiers & Mandatory Action Thresholds:) Tj
T*
(- TIER 1 - EXTREME / UNACCEPTABLE RISK \(Red: 5C, 5D, 5E, 4D, 4E\): Immediate engineering redesign and at least one SIL-2 or SIL-3 Independent Protection Layer \(IPL\) plus full-capacity emergency relief required.) Tj
T*
(- TIER 2 - HIGH / ALARP RISK \(Orange: 5B, 4C, 3D, 3E\): Requires verified SIL-1/SIL-2 SIS interlock and mechanical safeguard.) Tj
T*
(- TIER 3 - MEDIUM RISK \(Yellow: 5A, 4B, 3C, 2D\): Manage with independent BPCS alarms and standard operating procedures.) Tj
T*
(- TIER 4 - LOW / ACCEPTABLE RISK \(Green: 4A, 3A, 3B, 2A-2C, 1A-1E\): Acceptable with routine maintenance.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
